.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt XTC_RUNTIME 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xtc_runtime_set_stack_size ,
.Nm xtc_runtime_get_stack_size ,
.Nm xtc_runtime_set_stack_reclaim ,
.Nm xtc_runtime_get_stack_reclaim ,
.Nm xtc_runtime_set_blocking_threads ,
.Nm xtc_runtime_get_blocking_threads ,
.Nm xtc_runtime_set_preempt_involuntary ,
.Nm xtc_runtime_get_preempt_involuntary ,
.Nm xtc_runtime_set_iowq_workers ,
.Nm xtc_runtime_get_iowq_workers ,
.Nm xtc_runtime_set_alloc_audit ,
.Nm xtc_runtime_get_alloc_audit ,
.Nm xtc_set_stack_size ,
.Nm xtc_stack_size ,
.Nm xtc_stack_reclaim_enable ,
.Nm xtc_stack_reclaim_disable ,
.Nm xtc_stack_reclaim_enabled ,
.Nm xtc_blocking_pool_size ,
.Nm xtc_preempt_set_involuntary ,
.Nm xtc_io_set_iowq_max_workers ,
.Nm xtc_alloc_audit_enable
.Nd process-global runtime knobs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xtc_runtime.h
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_runtime_set_stack_size "size_t bytes"
.Ft size_t
.Fn xtc_runtime_get_stack_size "void"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_runtime_set_stack_reclaim "size_t keep_bytes"
.Ft size_t
.Fn xtc_runtime_get_stack_reclaim "void"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_runtime_set_blocking_threads "int nthreads"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_runtime_get_blocking_threads "void"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_runtime_set_preempt_involuntary "int on"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_runtime_get_preempt_involuntary "void"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_runtime_set_iowq_workers "unsigned bound" "unsigned unbound"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_runtime_get_iowq_workers "unsigned *out_bound" "unsigned *out_unbound"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_runtime_set_alloc_audit "int on"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_runtime_get_alloc_audit "void"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These calls configure the process as a whole.
Each setter has a getter that reads back the value in force.
A knob read when the thing it sizes is created is set before that
.Pq Dq before first use ;
the others may change at any time.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fn xtc_runtime_set_stack_size
The default stack size of a fiber created afterward, in bytes, rounded
up to a whole page; any time.
.Dv XTC_E_INVAL
below 16 KiB.
The default is 64 KiB; a proc may ask for its own size
.Pq Xr xtc_proc 3 .
.It Fn xtc_runtime_set_stack_reclaim
A nonzero
.Fa keep_bytes
turns on reclamation of a parked fiber's unused stack tail, leaving
.Fa keep_bytes
mapped below its stack pointer; 0 turns it off; any time
.Pq Xr xtc_stack_reclaim 3 .
.Dv XTC_E_NOSYS
where the platform cannot reclaim, and it stays off.
The getter returns 0 when it is off.
Off by default.
.It Fn xtc_runtime_set_blocking_threads
Pin the blocking-offload pool
.Pq Xr xtc_blocking 3
at
.Fa nthreads
threads, 1 to 64, before its first use.
.Dv XTC_E_STATE
once the pool has started,
.Dv XTC_E_INVAL
out of range.
The getter returns 0 while the pool sizes itself, the default.
.It Fn xtc_runtime_set_preempt_involuntary
Turn signal-context preemption on or off
.Pq Xr xtc_preempt_involuntary 3 ;
any time.
.Dv XTC_E_NOSYS
where it is not supported, and it stays off.
Off by default.
.It Fn xtc_runtime_set_iowq_workers
The io_uring io-wq worker caps per ring, for bounded and unbounded
work; 0 leaves the kernel default for that class.
Before the rings are created
.Pq Xr xtc_io 3 .
Other backends record the values and ignore them.
The default is (4, 0).
.It Fn xtc_runtime_set_alloc_audit
Turn the per-proc allocation auditor on or off
.Pq Xr xtc_alloc_audit 3 ;
any time.
.Dv XTC_E_NOMEM
if its table cannot be allocated.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The int-returning setters return
.Dv XTC_OK
or the error named above.
The getters cannot fail.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
The library reads these variables, through its own environment
wrapper, and never while the simulator is running:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev XTC_TAIL_ENABLE
At startup, turns the tail ring on: any value other than
.Ql 0 ,
.Ql off
or
.Ql false
enables the scheduler source,
.Ql all
every source
.Pq Xr xtc_tail 3 .
.It Ev XTC_CTRL_FD
In a child started by
.Xr xtc_osproc 3
or
.Xr xtc_xproc 3 :
the number of its inherited control socket.
The parent sets it.
.It Ev XTC_AIO_FORCE_OFFLOAD
.Ql 1
sends every
.Xr xtc_aio 3
operation to the offload pool instead of the native backend; a
testing aid.
.It Ev PATH
.Xr xtc_osproc 3
searches it for a program named without a slash.
.It Ev TMPDIR , TMP , TEMP
The directory for temporary files, in that order.
.El
.Sh DEPRECATED
These names still work through the rest of 2.x and are
removed in 3.0; see
.Lk https://codeberg.org/gregburd/libxtc/src/branch/main/docs/deprecations.md docs/deprecations.md .
A rebuild that uses one warns.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fn xtc_set_stack_size
Use
.Fn xtc_runtime_set_stack_size .
.It Fn xtc_stack_size
Use
.Fn xtc_runtime_get_stack_size .
.It Fn xtc_stack_reclaim_enable
Use
.Fn xtc_runtime_set_stack_reclaim ;
keep_bytes 0 now means off; the old 0 (one page) is the page size.
.It Fn xtc_stack_reclaim_disable
Use
.Fn xtc_runtime_set_stack_reclaim ;
call it with 0.
.It Fn xtc_stack_reclaim_enabled
Use
.Fn xtc_runtime_get_stack_reclaim ;
nonzero (the keep margin) when on.
.It Fn xtc_blocking_pool_size
Use
.Fn xtc_runtime_set_blocking_threads ;
"too late" is XTC_E_STATE under the new name, XTC_E_INVAL under the old.
.It Fn xtc_preempt_set_involuntary
Use
.Fn xtc_runtime_set_preempt_involuntary .
.It Fn xtc_io_set_iowq_max_workers
Use
.Fn xtc_runtime_set_iowq_workers .
.It Fn xtc_alloc_audit_enable
Use
.Fn xtc_runtime_set_alloc_audit .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xtc_inspect 3 ,
.Xr xtc_blocking 3 ,
.Xr xtc_stack_reclaim 3 ,
.Xr xtc 7
.Sh HISTORY
The set and get pairs first appeared in xtc 2.2.0, replacing per-module
setters that remain as deprecated names until 3.0.
